    "sourceScript": "scripts/runway-that-stops-traffic.md",
    "_convention": "One scene-spec JSON per script, saved alongside it as <script-name>.scenes.json. Each beat's `duration` is intentionally omitted here -- build_video.js fills it in at render time from the ACTUAL measured length of that beat's generated narration WAV. Gibraltar is too small to be its own polygon in the 110m dataset (it renders as part of the Iberian coastline), so it uses the 'scenes that aren't a country' convention: gold markers + hand-drawn `lines` for the runway (east-west) and Winston Churchill Avenue (north-south) crossing it, near Gibraltar's real coordinates (36.14N, 5.35W)."
